{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/594328-merfolk","id":594328,"title":"Merfolk?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-17T19:16:39-07:00","id":594328,"title":"Merfolk?","content":"I know there were merfolk changlings in the old world of Darkness have they been transfered over or has anyone homebrewed anytthing for them? THanks bunches!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T19:29:24-07:00","id":594352,"title":"","content":"Given how Seemings (in 1e) and Kiths (moreso in 2e) are very versatile, with appearance traits listed only as suggestions, you can make a &quot;merfolk&quot; changeling pretty easily. It depends on how you want to portray them.<br /> <br /> In 1e, there's the Nixie (Beast), Swimmerskin (Beast), Waterborn (Elemental), Apsara (Elemental), and Water-Dweller (Ogre) Kiths that can obviously be refluffed into merfolkishness. With the options for Mixed Kith and Dual Kith, there's even more options. A Fairest Dual Kith (Draconic/Swimmerskin or Waterborn) could be an aquatic dragon-folk, or a cute seamonster-girl, for example.<br /> <br /> In 2e, I don't recall the list of Kiths, but I'm sure there's aquatic ones. With the independence of Kith and Seeming, it's just a matter of picking the appropriate &quot;watery fae&quot; Kith and then the Seeming that meshes with your desired &quot;flavor&quot; of merfolk; Ogre for a brutal underwater monster, Fairest for a charming seducer, Darkling for a manipulator, Elemental for a &quot;truly fae&quot; water-spirit, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T20:46:12-07:00","id":594390,"title":"","content":"Do you want your character to look like a merfolk? Yes? Okay, then they do.<br /> <br /> Even something unrelated like an Artist... As an artist, were you <a href=\"https://youtu.be/GC_mV1IpjWA?t=53\" target=\"_blank\">that guy playing drums on seashells</a> in your keeper's rendition of Under the Sea? Then it makes sense for you to have an aquatic appearance. Or for Seeming, let's avoid watery Elmentals and aquatic Beasts and pick... Ogre. Off the cuff, I picture someone who retreats into a swamp near the castle where they worked, then starts doing the movie monster thing on their keeper's servants until they get an opportunity to escape Arcadia completely. So more Swamp Thing than merfolk, but it goes to show that you can take on characteristics that aren't obviously related to your Seeming if they make sense with your manner of escape.<br /> <br /> Of course, if what you want is the ability to breath underwater, not just have an aquatic appearance, then you might want to choose an appropriate kith. I have no idea if that's something you'll be able to do with Contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T00:43:19-07:00","id":595464,"title":"","content":"yea you generally just have to apply the right Kith or Kiths to make a decent Merfolk. Nix, Swimmerskin, Waterborn, and Water-Dweller can be combined with the right Seemings to make Merfolk. You can pick one (or two) of those and apply them to whichever Kith best applies...Fairest often for typical pretty mermaids, Beasts or Ogres for more dangerous ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T15:04:06-07:00","id":596121,"title":"","content":"I asked a sort of similair question in this thread...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/572556-changelings-how-changed-can-you-look-be\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/572556-changelings-how-changed-can-you-look-be\"> Changelings, how changed can you look/be? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/572556-changelings-how-changed-can-you-look-be\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/572556-changelings-how-changed-can-you-look-be </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hey everyone! In the old versions of Changeling I remember seeing art of changelings with horns, tails, hoofs, and kinds of stuff that would be hidden by the mask, and quite neatly so. Even people with antler horns can put on a cap without it getting stuck in their horns and so on and so forth. I loved it, I </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Just how strange/non-human can you look? Can you go down the path of not having actual legs, but rather a pair of fins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T22:00:28-07:00","id":596494,"title":"","content":"Someone in that thread quoted The Limits of Transformation. You've gotta be humanoid, so actual legs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T20:27:51-07:00","id":597751,"title":"","content":"I let a player take the Paraplegic Flaw to represent her Dancer/Swimmerskin's lack of legs. She was bound to a wheelchair on land, but could swim like a <i>freak</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T15:10:55-07:00","id":600995,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay on response! I appreciate all of yours though! Is there nothing currently to give one a tail? &quot;the typical mermaid&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T03:38:05-07:00","id":601558,"title":"","content":"I am pretty sure you can have a tail, like a cat-tail or whatever, just like you can have horns etc. but it would seem that the general consesus is no on a fin or something similair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}